  "question": {
    "text": "A coil is placed perpendicular to a magnetic field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5000</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. When the field is changed to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3000</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, an induced emf of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is produced in the coil. If the diameter of the coil is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, then the number of turns in the coil is:",
